    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Tourism</span> is a growing area of commercial activity across the world, and Nigeria is richly endowed with natural, cultural, and historical attractions. This topic examines what tourism means, why it matters, and the tourist centres found across Nigeria.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Tourism</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Tourism</span> refers to the activity of travelling to and staying in places outside one\'s usual environment for leisure, business, or other purposes, usually for a limited period. People who engage in tourism are called <strong>tourists</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Importance of Tourism</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Benefit</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Foreign exchange earnings</td><td>Tourists spend money that brings foreign currency into the country</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Employment</td><td>Creates jobs in hotels, transport, tour guiding, crafts, and catering</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Government revenue</td><td>Taxes and levies from tourism-related businesses boost government income</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cultural exchange</td><td>Promotes understanding and appreciation between different cultures</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Infrastructure development</td><td>Encourages the building of roads, hotels, and airports</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Preservation of heritage</td><td>Encourages the protection of historical and natural sites</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Tourist Centres in Nigeria</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Tourist Centre</th><th>Location / Type</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Yankari National Park</td><td>Bauchi State — game reserve and warm springs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Obudu Mountain Resort</td><td>Cross River State — highland resort</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Olumo Rock</td><td>Abeokuta, Ogun State — historic rock formation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Zuma Rock</td><td>Niger State — large monolith along the Abuja-Kaduna road</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Osun-Osogbo Sacred Grove</td><td>Osun State — UNESCO World Heritage cultural site</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Argungu Fishing Festival</td><td>Kebbi State — cultural festival</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>National Museum, Lagos</td><td>Lagos State — historical and cultural artefacts</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Role of Tourism in Economic Development</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Tourism contributes to national development by diversifying the economy away from dependence on a single sector (such as oil), earning foreign exchange, generating employment, and stimulating investment in transportation, hospitality, and other supporting industries.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners often ask you to identify or match tourist centres to their states. Learn a handful of key examples (Yankari, Obudu, Olumo Rock, Zuma Rock, Osun-Osogbo Grove) along with their states.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Tourism involves travelling to places outside one\'s usual environment for leisure or other purposes. It benefits Nigeria through foreign exchange, employment, government revenue, and infrastructural and cultural development, and Nigeria has numerous natural and cultural tourist centres across its states.\n</div>\n  ',
