    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  No business runs itself. Someone must plan what needs to be done and organize the people and resources to do it. This lesson introduces the meaning and importance of management, focusing on two key functions: <span class="learn-keyword">planning</span> and <span class="learn-keyword">organizing</span>.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Management</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Management</span> is the process of planning, organizing, directing, and controlling the resources of a business (human, financial, physical, and information resources) to achieve set goals efficiently and effectively.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Importance of Management</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Good management ensures resources are used efficiently, goals are achieved, employees are properly coordinated, risks are minimized, and the business remains competitive and profitable.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Planning as a Function of Management</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Planning</span> is the process of setting goals or objectives for a business and deciding in advance the best course of action to achieve them. It involves forecasting, setting objectives, and developing strategies and budgets.</p>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Step in Planning</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Setting objectives</td><td>Deciding what the business wants to achieve</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Forecasting</td><td>Predicting future conditions that may affect the business</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Developing strategies</td><td>Deciding the best methods to achieve set objectives</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Budgeting</td><td>Allocating financial resources needed to carry out the plan</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Organizing as a Function of Management</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Organizing</span> is the process of arranging resources — people, tasks, and materials — into a coherent structure so that the plans made can be effectively carried out. It involves dividing work into tasks, grouping tasks into departments, assigning duties, and establishing lines of authority.</p>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect of Organizing</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Division of labor</td><td>Breaking work into smaller, manageable tasks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Departmentalization</td><td>Grouping related tasks into departments (e.g., sales, finance, production)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Delegation of authority</td><td>Assigning responsibility and decision-making power to individuals or teams</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Ensuring different departments and individuals work together harmoniously</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Planning always comes before organizing — you must first decide WHAT you want to achieve (planning) before deciding HOW resources and people will be arranged to achieve it (organizing).\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Management is the process of planning, organizing, directing, and controlling resources to achieve business goals. Planning involves setting objectives and deciding a course of action, while organizing involves arranging people and resources into a structure to carry out those plans.\n</div>\n  ',
