    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Modern commerce increasingly relies on <span class="learn-keyword">electronic and digital payment methods</span>, which offer speed and convenience over traditional cash and paper-based instruments. This lesson explores these modern methods and their significance.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Electronic/Digital Methods of Payment</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>ATM (Automated Teller Machine) card</td><td>A card linked to a bank account allowing cash withdrawal and payment at ATMs and POS terminals</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Point of Sale (POS) terminal</td><td>A device that allows customers to pay electronically using a debit/credit card at the point of purchase</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Electronic funds transfer (EFT)/Bank transfer</td><td>Direct transfer of money from one bank account to another using online or mobile banking</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Mobile money/Mobile banking</td><td>Payment services accessed via mobile phones, allowing transfers, bill payments, and purchases</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Credit card</td><td>A card allowing the holder to borrow funds up to a limit to make purchases, to be repaid later, often with interest</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Online/internet payment gateways</td><td>Platforms that process payments for goods and services purchased over the internet</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Advantages of Electronic Payment Methods</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Advantage</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Speed and convenience</td><td>Transactions can be completed quickly, anytime and anywhere with internet/network access</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reduced risk of theft</td><td>No need to carry large amounts of physical cash</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Easy record-keeping</td><td>Digital transactions are automatically recorded, aiding accounting and tracking</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Supports e-commerce</td><td>Enables online buying and selling of goods and services</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Disadvantages/Challenges of Electronic Payment</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Electronic payments require internet or network access (which can be unreliable), carry risks of fraud and cybercrime, may involve transaction fees, and can exclude people without access to banking services or smartphones (part of the digital divide).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Why Modern Payment Methods Matter to Commerce</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Electronic payment methods have significantly boosted the speed and efficiency of trade, supported the growth of e-commerce, and improved financial inclusion by making transactions easier and more accessible, especially with the rise of mobile money.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish a debit card (which uses your own money in your account) from a credit card (which lets you borrow up to a limit, repaid later with interest) — this distinction is commonly tested.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Modern payment methods include ATM cards, POS terminals, electronic funds transfers, mobile money, credit cards, and online payment gateways. These methods offer speed, convenience, and support for e-commerce, but also carry risks like fraud and dependence on network access.\n</div>\n  ',
